{"id":"000VUP","title":"Quintuple Circles (6x6 chaos)","author":"jwsinclair","solvedCount":3,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-02T23:53:59+00:00","posted":"Gestern, 22:30 Uhr","rules":"Quintuple Circles, by James Sinclair\n\nDivide the grid into six orthogonally-connected six-cell regions, and place the digits 1-6 once in each row, column, and region.\n\nA digit inside a white circle appears in one of the four cells surrounding that circle *or* indicates the number of regions that occupy at least one of those cells (or both).\n\nSudokuPad\n\nFor more chaos, I highly recommend the recently-released Chaotic Construction pack by Sudoku Skunkworks (organized by Myxo).\n\nThe pack includes about 40 puzzles, contributed by a long list of very talented setters. Most of the puzzles are grouped into pairs, with a smaller, more approachable one to demonstrate the ruleset, followed by a larger, tougher version. (This puzzle was made with the pack in mind, but isn't included in it because I couldn't find a good way to adapt the ruleset to a larger grid.)","solutionCode":"row four, with a dash (\"-\") indicating every region border","tags":["Sudoku","Quadruple (Variante)","Chaos Construction (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/james-sinclair/quintuple-circles","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/james-sinclair/quintuple-circles","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":6,"cols":6,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["overlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-02T23:53:59+00:00"}